-se.da.Beatrix


// Interaction between two performers in real-time MIDI or Csound
// Open "-da.Alan" in another tab!
// Read https://bolprocessor.org/interactions-in-midi-and-csound/ for explanations


// This one works with real-time MIDI, but not with real-time Csound, because the last note should be transferred, but Csound does not transfer note with duration > 0

[Alan is waiting, Beatrix sends her notes and waits for Alan's phrase. She ends the performance when receiving Alan's last note 'E3'] 
{2, C#4 Eb4 A4 G#4 C4 Bb4 F#4 G4 B4 D4 E4} _script(wait for E3 channel 1)


// This one works both in real-time MIDI and Csound because <<E0>> of duration 0 is sent (by Alan) to both Csound and MIDI

[Beatrix starts and waits for E1 which we won't hear because its velocity is 0] 
_script(wait for E1 channel 1) _transpose(24) _vel(60) E2 . D2 E2 . _vel(65) B2 D2 E2 . G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(70) F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(75) C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(77) G#2 C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(80) A2 G#2 C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(85) Eb2 A2 G#2 C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(87) C#2 Eb2 A2 G#2 C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(90) F2 C#2 Eb2 A2 G#2 C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 _script(MIDI send Stop)


// This one works both in real-time MIDI and Csound

[Beatrix starts first and is waiting for Alan to send Start after playing some notes. Then she plays her part and sends Continue to Alan who will play more notes] 
_script(wait for Start) E4 D4 C4 _script(MIDI send Continue) _script(wait for Stop)